<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lian Po</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lian Po was a leading general of the State of Zhao in the 3rd century BCE, known for victories over Qi and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a>. At Changping in 260 BCE he held a defensive line against Qin until Zhao replaced him with Zhao Kuo, whose army was destroyed. His reconciliation with the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lin-xiangru">Lin Xiangru</a>, when he came to apologise carrying thorns on his back, became a celebrated story.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lian-po.jpg" alt="Lian Po" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 馮夢龍 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%BB%89%E9%A0%97.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
